# Anchor gate retired-commit-row fixture

## Question

Does the retired `git log -1` row shape still pass the anchor gate?

## Answer

No. Both rows deliberately carry the retired commit-and-date grammar whose only live field was the object hash.

## Derivation trail

The test materializes live 12-character commit and object hashes in the retired row shape and requires a grammar rejection, so no map can quietly keep the duplicated literal.

Provenance: {{TODAY}} · sid deadbeef

